            <div xml:id="d94">

                <pb facs="0097" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg85"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.83/89: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-02T11:00:00+03:00">July 2, 1942—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 2—5:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1133. Department’s 649, June 30, 11 p.m. As already reported by me the question
                    has been raised as to an eventual departure of the Egyptian Government and the
                    British Ambassador has suggested removal to Khartoum. Up to last night no
                    decision had been taken by Egyptian Government although as previously stated
                    there are indications that it would remain.</p>
                <p>I had assumed that upon leaving Egypt my ultimate destination would be Jidda
                    pending further dispositions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
